<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Voxels. Audited state:
    * "voxels_prefs" SharedPreferences (AppBackupAgent.prefNames) - settings.
    * filesDir/datastore_default.preferences_pb (AppBackupAgent.datastoreNames) -
      the shared DataStoreUtils file, holding AchievementsManager unlocks and
      VoxelsSync state.
    * filesDir/worlds/<world-id>/ - one directory per world, containing
      world.json (name, seed, timestamps), player.json (position/inventory) and
      regions/c_<x>_<z>.dat, the saved chunks written by the Rust save layer
      (src/main/rust/src/world/save.rs).
    * cacheDir/*.wav — SoundFx generates its sound effects at runtime. The
      platform already excludes cacheDir from every backup, so no rule needed.

  Why regions/ is a problem for cloud backup: each chunk file is up to
  SECTIONS_PER_CHUNK * ~12 KB, and chunk_map.rs keeps a render distance of 12,
  so an explored world is easily hundreds of megabytes. Android Auto Backup has
  a ~25 MB per-app quota, and blowing it doesn't just drop the big files — it
  fails the backup for the entire app, silently taking voxels_prefs down with
  it.

  The rules format has no wildcards, so there is no way to keep
  worlds/<id>/world.json while dropping worlds/<id>/regions. Excluding the whole
  worlds tree from cloud-backup is the deliberate choice: a truncated world is
  actively worse than no world, because decode_chunk() treats an unreadable
  chunk as ungenerated and regenerates it from the seed, silently erasing
  whatever the player built there.

  Device transfer has no quota and runs over a direct local link, so worlds go
  across intact — that is the path that actually preserves builds.

  SCOPE: voxels declares android:backupAgent=".platform.AppBackupAgent" and does
  NOT set android:fullBackupOnly, so Android uses key/value backup here and the
  <cloud-backup> section below is NOT consulted today. In practice the outcome
  matches the intent anyway: AppBackupAgent lists prefNames = ["voxels_prefs"]
  and datastoreNames = ["datastore_default"], so settings and achievements reach
  the cloud and saved worlds do not. The exclusion below is kept so that stays
  true if the backupAgent is ever removed and Auto Backup takes over.
  <device-transfer> IS governed by this file.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <!-- Not consulted while android:backupAgent is declared; see SCOPE above. -->
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="root" path="." />
        <include domain="file" path="." />
        <!-- Saved worlds: far over the 25 MB cloud quota, and a partial restore
             regenerates terrain from the seed and destroys player builds. -->
        <exclude domain="file" path="worlds" />
        <include domain="database" path="." />
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <include domain="external" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="root" path="." />
        <!-- Worlds included: no quota on D2D, and this is the only path that
             migrates a player's builds. -->
        <include domain="file" path="." />
        <include domain="database" path="." />
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <include domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
